{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a persistent loopback-only Unbound caching DNS resolver on node1. System applications now use 127.0.0.1, external DNS is forwarded through the existing upstream, and the configuration survived a verified node reboot.","actions_performed":["Installed Unbound and DNS diagnostic tools.","Configured Unbound to listen on TCP/UDP 127.0.0.1:53 and forward external queries to 10.100.99.1.","Enabled Unbound in the OpenRC default runlevel.","Set /etc/resolv.conf to 127.0.0.1 and prevented DHCP from overwriting it.","Verified external resolution and demonstrated cache misses followed by cache hits.","Safely rebooted node1 and verified full DNS recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Local caching DNS resolver for system applications","command_ids":["cmd-3b7de89b3bb8409e","cmd-a6c8a07eaf56468e","cmd-be8f6efef3f0417e"],"summary":"Configuration validates; system resolver points to 127.0.0.1; Unbound is enabled, running, and listening on TCP/UDP port 53."},{"requirement":"Normal external resolution and effective caching","command_ids":["cmd-7a7be2cb12064622","cmd-be8f6efef3f0417e","cmd-58f55079346a4627"],"summary":"Public DNS answers succeeded through 127.0.0.1. Repeated queries changed Unbound counters from miss to hit and returned in 0 ms on the cached lookup, both before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-be8f6efef3f0417e","cmd-ad7c56eb293f4ed3","cmd-18926650599c4dbf","cmd-58f55079346a4627"],"summary":"Healthy baseline used boot ID b1d6d308-6c42-4338-a480-b39f99e9ba0f; reboot was acknowledged; node returned with boot ID ffcf2405-b600-4e5a-bb3c-1c4f621f56ff; enabled service, listener, resolver configuration, external answers, and cache hits all recovered."}]}
